---
// /prototypes/setup/spatial-areas: the Spatial areas milestone, as a walk.
//
// Answers to docs/product-brief.md § 5, for this screen:
//   WHO         Dana, the tenant admin, standing the program up alone or beside
//               the account team; often without a GIS analyst on staff.
//   DOING WHAT  Naming the areas the portfolio is reported by, the subbasins a
//               board asks "what have you done in", and answering once where
//               their boundaries come from and what happens to a project outside
//               all of them.
//   BRINGING    An annual report whose map already names the subbasins; a sense
//               of which other areas matter; maybe a GIS person, maybe not.
//   OPTIMIZING  Confirming what the report already said over typing it; one
//               question a screen; area totals that account for every project.
//   PAYS FOR    dbo.GeospatialArea rows (a name and a kind, the layer
//               dbo.GeospatialAreaType), and two program preferences: the
//               map layer the boundaries come from and the outside policy.
//   LEAVES OUT  The geometry itself, a project's location and area membership,
//               and the layer ceiling. See below.
//
// FROM THE TEAMMATE'S 2026-09-23 "FIVE DOORS" MOCK, KEPT: its three decisions
// and its point-only outcome. What fills the blank in "What have you done in
// ___?"; where the boundaries come from, a file, a map service, a published
// source because "watersheds, counties, districts and tribal lands are all
// published free", or "our GIS person has it", a handoff that blocks nothing;
// and what happens to a project in none of the areas, a catch-all so "every
// project is accounted for", or blank, where "your area totals will quietly be
// short". And the answer "people just want it on a map": "A pin per project. The
// right answer with no GIS analyst."
//
// ALIGNED TO START'S WALK, 2026-09-23. (a) The KINDS were already asked by
// Start's intent `map` question (Watersheds, Counties, Our own boundaries), so
// this walk does not ask what "where" means again; each area carries a kind.
// (b) Area names come from the tenant's uploaded documents like every other
// milestone (the annual report's map names four subbasins), not from a service
// catalog. (c) The boundary source and the outside policy are two program-level
// preference screens, not a branch per area. (d) Point locations only is not a
// separate exit: it is the honest outcome of an empty roster, and the milestone
// confirms with zero areas once both preferences are answered.
//
// FOUR SCREENS. The documents' areas as tiles, one question over the whole cast;
// the map layer; the outside policy; the roster and Go to setup. The
// format is the Classifications walk's, with two preference screens where it
// has one.
//
// 2026-09-24: MANUAL ADD REMOVED, PUBLISHED AND SERVICE MERGED, A LAYER PICKER
// WITH A PREVIEW. On the teammate's feedback: an area typed by hand is a name
// with no geometry, so nothing can fall inside it, and the add screen is gone;
// "use a published source" and "connect a map service" were one answer, since a
// published source is a map service. The layer screen now offers the public
// layers the teammate's mock listed (USGS watersheds at three levels, Census
// counties, BIA tribal lands, Census congressional districts), the program's
// own service or file, and the GIS handoff. At Andy's direction the pressed
// layer draws on a Leaflet map with the confirmed areas filled in, so the
// tenant sees whether the layer holds the areas their report named.
//
// PRODUCT WORK, NOT BUILT HERE. The mock's five-layer ceiling ("Five is the
// ceiling. Each one costs a reporter nothing: a project's areas are worked out
// from its location"): the ceiling is a platform limit, and the walk names areas,
// not layers. The file upload and the sync from the chosen layer, where the
// geometry arrives. The GIS handoff link ("They get a link back to this question with
// your answers intact"). Area membership is computed on the project record, so
// no screen here asks a reporter anything.
import SetupLayout from '../../../layouts/SetupLayout.astro';
import Firma2SetupStepper from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-stepper.astro';
import Firma2SetupAreaPicker from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-area-picker.astro';
import Firma2SetupAreaLayer from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-area-layer.astro';
import Firma2SetupAreaOutside from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-area-outside.astro';
import Firma2SetupAreaRoster from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-area-roster.astro';
import EsaBadge from '@esa/ecology/esa-badge.astro';
import type { SetupStep } from '../../../lib/setup-steps';

const steps: SetupStep[] = [
  { id: 'suggested', label: 'Suggested' },
  { id: 'layer', label: 'Boundaries' },
  { id: 'outside', label: 'Outside all areas' },
  { id: 'review', label: 'Review' },
];
const stepIds = steps.map((step) => step.id);
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: stack(2xl)
  sections:
    - status counts  -> esa-badge   (two, slotted into the milestone band SetupLayout renders)
    - walk           -> firma2-setup-stepper
      - suggested      -> firma2-setup-area-picker
      - layer          -> firma2-setup-area-layer   (with firma2-map-preview)
      - outside        -> firma2-setup-area-outside
      - review         -> firma2-setup-area-roster
-->
<SetupLayout title="Spatial areas" width="wide" milestone="spatial-areas">
  <!-- The counts the screens produce, at the top of the page. Synced by the
       script below from the same draft the screens read. -->
  <span slot="status" data-part="confirmed-count"><EsaBadge value="0 confirmed" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>
  <span slot="status" data-part="review-count"><EsaBadge value="0 to review" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>

  <Firma2SetupStepper steps={steps} stepIds={stepIds}>
    <Firma2SetupAreaPicker />
    <Firma2SetupAreaLayer />
    <Firma2SetupAreaOutside />
    <Firma2SetupAreaRoster />
  </Firma2SetupStepper>
</SetupLayout>

<script>
  import { listSpatialAreas } from '../../../lib/setup-draft';

  const confirmedBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="confirmed-count"] .esa-badge__text');
  const reviewBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="review-count"] .esa-badge__text');

  const sync = (): void => {
    const records = listSpatialAreas();
    const confirmed = records.filter((record) => record.status === 'confirmed').length;
    const toReview = records.filter((record) => record.status === 'suggested').length;

    if (confirmedBadge) confirmedBadge.textContent = `${confirmed} confirmed`;
    if (reviewBadge) reviewBadge.textContent = `${toReview} to review`;
  };

  document.addEventListener('setup-draft-change', sync);
  sync();
</script>
